        <body>
            <div xml:id="d78">

                <pb facs="0276" n="240" sameAs="frus:frus1969-76v06/pg240"/>

                <head>78. Memorandum From the President’s Assistant for National Security Affairs
                        (Kissinger) to President
                        Nixon<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d78-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1969-06-04">June 4, 1969</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>
                        US Negotiating Team in Paris</item>
                </list>
                <pb facs="0277" n="241" xml:id="pg241"/>
                <p>Attached is a memorandum handed to me by Mel
                        Laird which offers some additional insights into the problems
                    within our Paris negotiating team. This memorandum was prepared by a high
                    ranking officer detailed to Paris (but not the source of the previous
                    statements).</p>


                <xi:include href="d78-a1.xml" xpointer="d78-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
